@startuml
title File Operations (extract · copy · delete · paste · rename)

start

:User selects node(s) in the tree
and triggers an operation;

:Controller dispatches the file operation
to the active session;

if (action is copy or cut?) then (yes)
  :Record selected node(s) and
  source session in clipboard;
  stop
endif

:Resolve file operations strategy
for the active session;
note right
  Remote and local sessions each have
  their own strategy implementation.
  The controller depends only on the
  shared interface (Dependency Inversion).
end note

if (operation?) then (extract)
  :Copy file(s) to chosen local destination;
  if (source is remote?) then (yes)
    :Stream file bytes from remote session;
    :Write to local destination;
  else (no)
    :Copy across filesystem boundary;
  endif

else if (delete) then (yes)
  :Delete path from active session;
  if (directory?) then (yes)
    :Recursively delete all contents first;
  endif

else if (paste) then (yes)
  :Read bytes from clipboard source session;
  :Write bytes into active session target;
  if (was cut?) then (yes)
    :Delete original from source session;
  endif

else (rename)
  :Rename path within active session;
endif

if (success?) then (yes)
  :Refresh tree view for affected session(s);
else (no)
  :Show error message to user;
endif

stop
@enduml
